+## Notes
+
+Validation performed 2026-11-16 against `spec.md` as written. All items pass. Two deliberate
+decisions are recorded here so a reviewer does not mistake them for oversights:
+
+1. **Platform constraints are restated on purpose** (FR-019 names Python 3.11+, the standard
+   library, the existing `src/bookmarks` package; FR-020 names pytest). These are not design
+   choices made by this specification — they are pre-existing constraints imposed by the project
+   constitution (Principles I and III) and by feature `001-bookmark-manager-cli` (`001:FR-025`,
+   `001:FR-026`, `001:FR-027`), restated so every constitutional gate has a requirement to trace
+   to. No module layout, function design, library or algorithm is specified anywhere in the spec.
+
+2. **File shapes and the page layout are contract, not implementation.** The CSV header line, the
+   JSON record keys and the exact HTML page in FR-012 are the feature's externally visible
+   interface — the user supplies and reads those exact bytes — and are specified to the byte for
+   the same reason the earlier feature's export formats were. The spec says what the bytes must be,
+   never how they are produced or parsed.
+
+Judgment calls that the feature description left open were resolved as reasonable defaults and
+recorded in the spec's **Assumptions** section rather than as `[NEEDS CLARIFICATION]` markers.
+The three worth a second look during planning or review are:
+
+- A record whose address fails the `http://`/`https://` rule aborts the whole import with status 2
+  (FR-010, FR-011), rather than being skipped — driven by "imports nothing" in the description and
+  by constitution Principle II, which forbids skipping a bad record to keep running.
+- Problems with the import **file** are status 2, never status 1, which stays reserved for the
+  collection's own storage file (FR-017).
+- Values drawn from the collection are HTML-escaped in the web-page export (FR-014), so a title
+  containing `&` or `<` yields a well-formed page. The description's example output is unchanged
+  by this.
+
+Items marked incomplete would require spec updates before `/speckit-clarify` or `/speckit-plan`;
+none are.
